r Honors), possibly already counted? Actually patterns: Dragon Pung (not, it's wind), Prevalent Wind (yes, 2 pts), Seat Wind (yes, 2 pts), Pung of Terminals or Honors (yes, 1 pt). But these may overlap? In scoring, you sum fan values. Prevalent Wind and Seat Wind are separate 2-fan patterns, and Pung of Terminals or Honors is 1 fan. So from that F4 pung alone you have at least 2+2+1 = 5 fan guaranteed if you win. Plus possibly other patterns.  \\n\\nYou need at least 8 fan total. So you need additional 3+ fan from rest of hand.  \\n\\nYour hand: W2, W3x3, W4, B4, B5, F2. If you keep the W3 pung (concealed), that's a concealed pung (maybe 2 fan for Two Concealed Pungs if you have another concealed pung? You don't yet). But W3 pung is simple tiles (no honors/terminals), so only All Simples (2 fan) if entire hand has no terminals/honors except F4 pung? Wait F4 pung is honors, so All Simples is out.  \\n\\nBetter plan: try to go for Half Flush (only honors and one suit) \\u2014 you have W suit tiles (W2, W3, W4) and honors (F4 pung, F2). If you discard B4 and B5, you're left with only W suit and honors. That's Half Flush (6 fan) if you win with only W and honors. Plus you already have Prevalent Wind + Seat Wind on F4 pung (4 fan), plus Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 fan) = 5 fan, plus Half Flush 6 fan = 11 fan total, enough. So discarding B4 and B5 ASAP is good.  \\n\\nRight now you have B4 and B5 \\u2014 discard one now, then later discard the other. Which to discard first? B4 and B5 are both simple tiles, no big difference. But see opponents' discards: previous player played B4 earlier (game history: Play B4). That might make B4 safer to discard? But also next player history shows Play B2, Play F4. Not much info.  \\n\\nAlso consider your W tiles: you have W2, W3x3, W4. You could aim for Pure Shifted Pungs if you get W2 pung and W4 pung? Unlikely with only 1 W2 and 1 W4. Alternatively, keep W3 pung for All Pungs (6 fan) if you get two more pungs. But you have only 6 hand tiles left after melds, so to get two more pungs you'd need specific draws.  \\n\\nGiven Half Flush is promising, discard a bamboo suit tile now. Between B4 and B5, B5 is middle tile, slightly more useful to others for chows, but B4 is also. Since previous player discarded B4, maybe B4 is slightly safer. But not critical.  \\n\\nAlso, you have F2 single \\u2014 could be pair for winning, but F2 is not prevalent/seat wind (prevailing wind is North F4, seat wind North F4). So F2 only useful as pair or pung if you get two more. But you have only one. Discarding F2 might be safe too, but keeping it gives chance for All Types (6 fan) if you keep B suit? Actually All Types requires all three suits + winds + dragons. You already have W suit, B suit, F wind, no dragons yet. But you have no T suit. So All Types not possible unless you get T suit. Unlikely.  \\n\\nSo best: discard B4 or B5. Choose B4 because it was discarded before by previous player, possibly indicating they don't need B4.  \\n\\nBut also check: you have W2 and W4 \\u2014 with W3x3, you could use W2 and W4 with extra W1 or W5 to form chows. But W1 is in your meld already, so only one W1 left in wall (unshown tiles show W1:2 total, but one is in your meld? Actually unshown tiles count includes all tiles not visible to you? It says \\\"Unshown tiles are: [W1: 2; ...]\\\" meaning there are 2 W1 tiles left in wall + others' hands. Since your meld used one W1, and there were 4 total, so 2 left. So possible to get W1. Similarly W5: 4 left. So chows possible.  \\n\\nBut Half Flush plan seems more straightforward.  \\n\\nAlso, you have 3 W3 \\u2014 if you discard one W3, you break up the pung, but maybe you need to keep pair? Actually you have 3 W3, that's a pung already, you can declare it as kong if you draw 4th? But kong would expose it unless concealed kong. But you might not want to expose if going for concealed hand. But you already have two exposed melds, so Fully Concealed Hand not possible.  \\n\\nGiven all, discard B4 to move toward Half Flush.  \\n\\nReason: Discarding B4 removes a tile from an unwanted suit (Bamboo) to pursue Half Flush (only W suit and honors), which combined with your already strong F4 pung (Prevalent Wind + Seat Wind) can yield 11+ fan, meeting the 8-fan requirement easily. B4 is relatively safe based on previous discard history.  \\n\\nAnswer: Play B4\"}"}
